kelly-cs: forwarding customer report — TypeScript/Node SDK streaming in edge runtime shows out-of-order chunks (ReadableStream). Happens after token rotation/retry. Customer sees chunk sequence gaps and occasional 402 billing errors after retries. Repro included below.

jordan-dev: thanks — can you paste the minimal repro and the SDK version/runtime details? also last_request_id if available.

kelly-cs: putting the snippet the customer used. environment: Vercel Edge, @redwood/sdk v1.8.3, node target: edge.

kelly-cs: ```ts
import { createClient } from '@redwood/sdk';
const client = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const res = await client.chat.stream({ model: 'open-llama-13b', messages: [{role:'user', content:'stream test'}] });
const reader = res.body.getReader();
while (true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  console.log('chunk', value.toString());
}
```

kelly-cs: console output example:
"chunk seq=1 data=hello"
"chunk seq=3 data=world"
"chunk seq=2 data=there"

maya-eng: hmm. two quick asks: 1) is SDK actually the latest? there was a streaming reorder bug fixed in v1.8.5 that affected edge runtimes when token refresh triggered concurrent fetches. 2) can you confirm whether the token rotation flow (short-lived credential refresh) runs in the same execution context as the original request?

jordan-dev: also, please enable debug logs: set DEBUG=rdw:stream and capture the logs + the request id header x-rdw-request-id. that helps correlate queueing + retry behavior.

kelly-cs: they sent logs and last_request_id: rq_20260317_09abcc. Attach: (trimmed)
`[rdw:stream] open stream id=rq_20260317_09abcc seq=1`
`[rdw:stream] token rotate start id=rq_20260317_09abcc`
`[rdw:stream] retry spawn id=rq_20260317_09abcc child=1`
`[rdw:stream] chunk seq=1 id=rq_20260317_09abcc`
`[rdw:stream] chunk seq=3 id=rq_20260317_09abcc`
`[rdw:stream] chunk seq=2 id=rq_20260317_09abcc`

sam-sre: deployment history — deploy-bot shows a small streaming runtime patch rolled out ~10m before this request. deploy-bot: `rollout edge-stream-kernel v20260317-4f2a`

deploy-bot: rollout started 2410996500, 30% -> 100% completed 2410999800.

billing-bot: customer reported duplicate small charges after retries; we saw a 402 transient returned then a retry that succeeded — billing system charged the retry. need to check idempotency keys.

maya-eng: likely root cause: concurrent token refresh triggered new upstream fetch with different connection window; streaming kernel merged chunks from the old and new connections without preserving original sequence. workaround: pin token scope to avoid refresh mid-stream or disable rotation for long-lived streams. we're preparing a hotfix.

jordan-dev: short-term triage steps for us / customer to try:
- verify SDK version: `npm ls @redwood/sdk` (recommend v1.8.6+ if available)
- reproduce with `VERCEL_REGION=iad vercel dev --edge` or local `wrangler dev` if using Cloudflare Workers
- enable DEBUG=rdw:stream and capture logs for request id
- if using token rotation, try toggling to static key to confirm behavior
- collect a packet capture (if possible) or proxy via `ngrok` to capture SSE frames order

maya-eng: quick repro snippet to run locally (edge-like):
```js
// edge-repro.js (run with node 18+ experimental fetch)
import http from 'http';
import fetch from 'node-fetch'; // poly if needed
http.createServer(async (req, res) => {
  const r = await fetch('https://api.redwood.example/stream', { headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + process.env.RW_KEY } });
  r.body.pipe(res);
}).listen(8787);
```

k elly-cs: customer tried switching to hosted endpoint and saw ordering fixed, but they can't move off edge due to latency needs. they asked for ETA on fix and whether there's a config flag to avoid billing duplicates.

maya-eng: ETA: hotfix patch targeted for v20260317-5a10 in the next 24 hours. For billing duplicates: add idempotency key `x-rdw-idempotency: <client-generated>` on initial request; server will dedupe charged retries for this flow — ops needs to verify for streaming flows specifically.

jordan-dev: if the customer can reproduce reliably, escalate: include DEBUG logs, request id, SDK version, and a minimal repro (the edge-repro.js or the Vercel snippet). I'll open an ENG escalation ticket and link it to the deploy roll.

kelly-cs: will ask customer to capture logs and try static key test. I'll update thread when they reply. thanks. :thumbsup:
